<title>USA: Union machinists ratify Air Wisconsin agreement.</title>
<headline>Union machinists ratify Air Wisconsin agreement.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM) said Thursday its members approved a mid-term wage adjustment with Air Wisconsin, a unit of UAL Corp.</p>
<p>The agreement, which was tentatively approved by the commuter carrier and the IAM in December, covers nearly 400 union workers at Air Wisconsin, the IAM said.</p>
<p>The current contract, signed in 1994, is scheduled to expire in 2000, the union said.</p>
<p>UAL shares were shares were off 1-1/8 at 71-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
